.DS_Store

# `caf dev` GENERATES this from cafaye.yml and rewrites it on every run — the
# file says so in its own first line ("Do not edit: every run rewrites this
# file"). It is build output shaped like a source file, which is why it needs
# saying here rather than relying on it being untracked by accident: an
# untracked generated file is one `git add -A` away from being committed, and
# from there it is a merge conflict nobody can resolve by reading it.
#
# pantry is the registry rather than a service and holds no docker-compose.yml,
# so there is no hand-written counterpart here to confuse it with.
/caf.dev.compose.yaml
